WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:25.820
So, this course on Software Engineering. Now, we will just have a brief introduction to various

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:32.100
issues in Software Engineering, motivation, why we need to study this course, what are

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:42.810
the benefits that will accrue from here and so on. So, let us get started. First is about

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:54.000
myself, I will be the instructor for this course. My name is Rajip Mal, completed all my

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:01.920
education bachelors, masters, PhD from the Indian Institute of Science, Bangalore that

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:12.420
is quite some years back. That is the institute where I graduated and then worked few years

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:23.220
with Motorola India and then have been with IIT Kharagpur since 1994 and currently a professor

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:29.940
at the CAC department. So, that is the institute Indian Institute of Technology Kharagpur.

00:01:35.710 --> 00:01:45.530
To start with any course, we need to know what the course deals with, we will also do the

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:53.030
same thing, we will start with the basic definition of Software Engineering. If somebody asks that

00:01:53.030 --> 00:02:04.270
what is Software Engineering, we should be able to answer based on this. The simplest

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:11.190
answer, what is Software Engineering is an engineering approach to develop software.

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:20.080
But then the question arises that what exactly is the engineering approach to develop software,

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:31.520
how is it different from traditional approach to develop software. To appreciate this distinction

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:39.820
between the engineering approach to develop software and traditional novice approach to

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:45.880
develop software, we will just look at a analogy with a building construction.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:57.650
Let us say you want to construct a building, what would you do? First let us consider that you

00:02:57.650 --> 00:03:05.870
want to build a small wall like this, that you will be very easily be able to do from your

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:16.620
basic intuition that you need some bricks, cement, color and so on and you will succeed

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:24.460
in developing a good small wall like this. But let us say you are now asked to build

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:36.590
a large building like this having 30, 40 floors a complex. Your basic intuition about construction

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:46.050
will not work here. If you actually get started building this with your basic intuition building

00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:58.880
may collapse, it will never complete, it will be of poor quality and so on. The same

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:07.040
thing is with respect to software. If somebody is asked to write a small program let us

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:14.780
say 10, 20, 50 lines of code, he will be able to do it based on his basic intuition. But

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:26.910
let us consider developing a software which is 100,000 lines of code. Now if you wants

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:37.170
to extend the intuition and develop a large software, again you will face the same fate

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:44.870
as constructing a large building from the basic intuition. The engineering approach to develop

00:04:44.870 --> 00:05:00.550
software lets one to develop software based on some techniques and tools. So, we will look

00:05:00.550 --> 00:05:08.980
at those techniques and tools as part of the software engineering. So, an alternate

00:05:08.980 --> 00:05:17.980
definition of software engineering can be that it is a collection of past experience which has

00:05:17.980 --> 00:05:26.380
resulted in various techniques for development of large software, methodologies for development

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:41.840
and some guidelines and tools. As we proceed with this course we will be clear about what

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:47.180
are the techniques, what are the methodologies and guidelines, tools and so on.

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:57.460
Now let us look at the IEEE definition of what software engineering is. The IEEE definition

00:05:57.460 --> 00:06:05.860
is software engineering is the application of systematic, disciplined, quantifiable approach

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:14.780
to the development, operation and maintenance of software and that is the application of

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:21.940
engineering to software. So, the IEEE definition also says that software

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:29.850
engineering is the engineering approach to develop software and it further elaborates

00:06:29.850 --> 00:06:46.230
this by saying application of systematic, disciplined, quantifiable approach and all

00:06:46.230 --> 00:06:57.960
developed from experience of programmers over the last several years. To motivate the need

00:06:57.960 --> 00:07:05.240
for software engineering why it is important for the software developers to learn software

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:13.080
engineering let us just understand what the software crisis is because everybody says

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:27.320
that there is a software crisis. The software crisis the symptoms are that they fail to meet

00:07:27.320 --> 00:07:40.260
user requirements. Software is delivered and then the users feel that it is not what they

00:07:40.260 --> 00:07:48.940
wanted. Software is expensive, much more expensive than hardware and every year the

00:07:48.940 --> 00:07:55.840
difference between software and hardware prices have been increasing. It is difficult to make

00:07:55.840 --> 00:08:04.260
any changes to the software to debug. If there is a problem reported it takes long time to

00:08:04.260 --> 00:08:15.630
correct it sometimes the bugs cannot be corrected. Difficult to enhance add new features it

00:08:15.630 --> 00:08:26.640
is very usual for software to be delivered late and use resources non-optimally. For most

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:36.620
of the software that you order or develop as part of project have these symptoms that

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:43.880
they rarely meet the user requirements turn out to be very expensive, difficult to alter

00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:49.080
debug and enhance delivered late and use resources non-optimally.

00:08:51.620 --> 00:09:04.400
Just to explain how expensive is the software compared to hardware over the years if we compute

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:12.740
how much a company spent on hardware and how much it spent on software. If we plot the

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:20.740
ratio we will see that 1960s are and so the hardware was the major expense millions of

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:30.350
dollars of hardware and then software was very inexpensive compared to the hardware.

00:09:32.990 --> 00:09:49.230
But then the hardware costs have dropped dramatically and software costs have risen. So now the

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:58.340
hardware cost divided by software cost is almost nominal approaching 0. Just to give a feel just

00:09:58.840 --> 00:10:05.200
let us say that a laptop or test of costs 45000 rupees and let us say some software let us

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:14.280
say rational. It costs 3 lakh rupees if it is not locked and floating license cost 6

00:10:14.280 --> 00:10:25.100
lakh rupees which runs on a desktop. So just see that the cost of one software is many times

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:30.420
the cost of the hardware and then we need to run various types of software on the hardware.

00:10:32.100 --> 00:10:43.180
So now the software is much more expensive. Companies spend much more on software than

00:10:43.180 --> 00:10:50.780
on hardware. But then the question arises is that why is that the cost of hardware has dropped so

00:10:50.780 --> 00:10:58.800
much but then software has not really the cost has not dropped and actually increased.

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:09.140
There are many reasons for this. We will examine the reasons but before that we just

00:11:09.140 --> 00:11:18.980
want to ask a very fundamental question that if hardware is so good it is delivered in time

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:29.620
extremely reliable inexpensive then why not have everything in hardware because after all

00:11:29.620 --> 00:11:38.220
whatever can be done by software can also be done by hardware. There must be some reasons

00:11:39.100 --> 00:11:45.560
otherwise people would only be developing hardware and using it and there would be no software.

00:11:46.860 --> 00:11:56.040
Let us look at the reasons why software is indispensable and actually the use of software

00:11:56.040 --> 00:12:07.700
is increasing as compared to hardware. There are 2 or 3 major virtues or strong points of

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:23.360
software which actually make it a preferred solution compared to hardware. One of the most

00:12:23.360 --> 00:12:35.020
important thing is that developing software is easy, faster and also if you find anything

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:46.060
to be changed you can easily change it hardware development is a long drawn process. If it is

00:12:46.060 --> 00:12:53.440
a VLSI chip that you are considering then it is multi-year starting from requirements

00:12:53.440 --> 00:13:03.160
to fabrication it is a long process. And if you later want to make a small change

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:12.340
again you have to make that long process change requirements change design mask and so on fabricate

00:13:12.340 --> 00:13:22.360
test. So, that is a long duration several years compared to software making a fix a

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:33.680
small change may be just a few days and also software consumes no space weight or power.

00:13:35.280 --> 00:13:44.040
If you want to develop something that works in software let us say rational enterprise suit

00:13:44.040 --> 00:13:50.940
let us consider any software or maybe let us say the word processing software let us consider

00:13:50.940 --> 00:14:02.120
Microsoft word. It is possible to have this developed in hardware, but then the size of

00:14:02.120 --> 00:14:09.840
the hardware will be enormous. It will be extremely expensive and it will consume huge power,

00:14:11.140 --> 00:14:18.180
but then if you as software it just resides in your hard disk and just gets executed

00:14:18.180 --> 00:14:24.640
feature by feature and that is the reason why software is the preferred mode of solution for

00:14:24.640 --> 00:14:39.700
applications as compared to hardware. But then one thing we need to appreciate that software

00:14:39.700 --> 00:14:50.220
is becoming more complex and as we change software it also the complexity increases.

00:14:55.850 --> 00:15:01.950
But then what is the basic reason? We are trying to answer some fundamental questions here and as

00:15:01.950 --> 00:15:09.090
we proceed these questions are actually the basics based on which the other techniques are built up

00:15:09.750 --> 00:15:18.170
must understand these basic principles that the more complex is the software the harder it

00:15:18.170 --> 00:15:24.910
is to change and also if we change it the complexity of the software further increases.

00:15:25.590 --> 00:15:35.990
What is the reason? The main reason is that to change a software we must first understand it

00:15:36.850 --> 00:15:42.510
without understanding how it works where exactly we have to change we cannot change it

00:15:44.140 --> 00:15:52.020
and if it is very complex software will take lot of effort to understand and then make the

00:15:52.020 --> 00:16:05.970
change and also if we make a small change it changes the basic underlying design modularity

00:16:05.970 --> 00:16:14.830
and so on as we will see later that every change actually degrades the structure of

00:16:14.830 --> 00:16:21.350
the software and makes it much more complex for somebody else to understand as changes

00:16:21.350 --> 00:16:27.790
keep on happening to a software may be due to additional features to be supported may be

00:16:27.790 --> 00:16:37.130
to correct bugs and so on the software becomes more complex becomes much more difficult for

00:16:37.130 --> 00:16:44.630
somebody to understand and make further changes. This is one of the very basic principles as

00:16:44.630 --> 00:16:52.790
we proceed will need these principles and it will help us understand why some techniques

00:16:53.290 --> 00:17:00.760
are the way that they are. Now let us look at the large number of projects

00:17:00.760 --> 00:17:12.440
that are done what is the statistics about the success rate of the projects. The success

00:17:12.440 --> 00:17:29.580
rate is very surprising that only a quarter is successful just 28% is successful a quarter

00:17:29.580 --> 00:17:39.940
is never sees the light of the day they are cancelled and half of the projects they

00:17:41.760 --> 00:17:55.090
are delayed delivered run delivered late and also the cost overrun the price increases.

00:17:57.040 --> 00:18:04.120
But then why is it that only quarter of the software is actually successful half of the

00:18:04.120 --> 00:18:09.960
software is challenged and another quarter is actually failure they are to be cancelled.

00:18:09.960 --> 00:18:30.400
Let us try to understand what is the reason the reasons are that now there is a demand

00:18:30.400 --> 00:18:39.400
for more and more software. The hardware is simpler and the software is much more complex

00:18:40.370 --> 00:18:45.440
due to obvious reason that any complexity in the application has to be done in the software

00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:52.500
because otherwise hardware will be very difficult to develop it will be large it will consume

00:18:52.500 --> 00:18:59.880
lots of power volume and so on. So, the problem sizes of software is increasing

00:18:59.880 --> 00:19:11.700
year after year poor project management because these are after all entirely manual efforts

00:19:12.400 --> 00:19:16.560
the programmers have to develop they have to write the code test and so on.

00:19:18.450 --> 00:19:25.430
But surprisingly one of the major reasons that has been identified for the software crisis

00:19:25.890 --> 00:19:34.080
is the lack of adequate training in software engineering. The developers they are not

00:19:34.900 --> 00:19:42.260
very convergent with the latest software engineering techniques. When they graduate

00:19:42.260 --> 00:19:48.080
from a college they do not have proper background in software engineering they have studied

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:58.020
some things that that do not really help in developing good quality software. There is a

00:19:58.020 --> 00:20:04.140
increasing skill shortage as far as software development software engineering principles

00:20:04.140 --> 00:20:11.040
are concerned and even with software engineering the skill improvements are not really very

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:19.880
drastic it improves moderately very slowly over the years compared to the way the

00:20:19.880 --> 00:20:24.940
problem sizes are increasing the productivity development has not really kept pace.

00:20:31.380 --> 00:20:40.500
Let us just try to understand another very basic aspect might have heard that somebody

00:20:40.500 --> 00:20:49.040
saying programming is an art, but then we said software engineering and there is

00:20:49.040 --> 00:20:55.620
an engineering approach to develop software. So, is software an art or engineering let

00:20:55.620 --> 00:21:05.230
us just try to understand the issues concerned. Now let us look at how the technology develops

00:21:05.850 --> 00:21:14.990
for any specific domain whether it is steel making whether it is paper making let us see

00:21:14.990 --> 00:21:24.400
how the technology develops. If we look at the technology development pattern initially

00:21:24.400 --> 00:21:34.760
somebody comes up with some idea and then follows it comes up with solution. Let us say paper

00:21:34.760 --> 00:21:43.840
making was known to some people in China and only they could develop good quality paper.

00:21:44.360 --> 00:21:51.350
The others tried they do not know how to make paper possibly came up with some very bad

00:21:51.350 --> 00:22:03.670
quality paper and they thought that paper making is an art. And artist as you know that if you ask

00:22:03.670 --> 00:22:11.970
somebody that how come he paints so well let us say an artist is a draws a nice drawing and you

00:22:11.970 --> 00:22:17.450
ask him how did you come up with such a nice drawing you will say that ok it just comes

00:22:17.450 --> 00:22:24.760
to me I just draw it like that. Same thing with technology initially they say that we

00:22:24.760 --> 00:22:33.140
just know how to make it, but then slowly the art form in technology development graduates

00:22:33.140 --> 00:22:43.960
to a craft form. In a craft form there are some techniques they can identify how they make it

00:22:44.780 --> 00:22:50.520
and they do not share it actually with lot of people they share with only their apprentice.

00:22:51.860 --> 00:22:59.380
It is basically a hidden secret let us say paper making or steel making they would not like to

00:22:59.380 --> 00:23:10.610
share with many people they know the techniques, but they do not share it and there are craftsmen

00:23:11.250 --> 00:23:18.250
who know how to do it. So, they are basically the apprentices and then they also share with

00:23:18.250 --> 00:23:29.090
very less number of people. And slowly it transits to an engineering approach. In engineering the

00:23:29.090 --> 00:23:39.720
techniques are all investigated the past experience is analyzed and scientific basis is given to

00:23:39.720 --> 00:23:51.680
these techniques. These are well documented and this can be studied by anybody these are open

00:23:51.680 --> 00:24:01.240
knowledge and then it has graduated into engineering. But what about program writing? Yes it is same

00:24:01.240 --> 00:24:11.100
pattern the program writing has followed. In the 1960s there were good programmers and there were

00:24:11.100 --> 00:24:21.840
bad programmers. The good programmers they just wrote good programs and they do not know

00:24:21.840 --> 00:24:27.260
how they write good programs, but then they just wrote good programs and the other programmers

00:24:27.260 --> 00:24:33.620
they just struggled and could not come up with good programs. But then slowly the techniques

00:24:33.620 --> 00:24:42.530
that they were using in writing the good programs were identified and shared with few and that

00:24:42.530 --> 00:24:48.990
was the craft form that good programmers could train other programmers who can become

00:24:48.990 --> 00:24:54.950
good programmers. But later the techniques that they were using for writing good programs

00:24:54.950 --> 00:25:04.010
were all systematically investigated scientific basis given to them and published in the literature

00:25:04.550 --> 00:25:10.370
in the book form and so on. So, that anybody can read and then it has graduated to an

00:25:10.370 --> 00:25:19.610
engineering firm where somebody can read what are required to really develop good software

00:25:19.610 --> 00:25:27.810
large software the basic principles one need to know and so on and our focus is looking

00:25:27.810 --> 00:25:38.440
at this software engineering techniques. If we look at the engineering approach to

00:25:38.440 --> 00:25:47.260
develop software there is heavy use of past experience the past experience is systematically

00:25:47.260 --> 00:26:01.500
arranged and for this experience investigation has been made theoretical basis and quantifiable

00:26:04.160 --> 00:26:10.900
techniques quantitative techniques have been provided, but then for many of the techniques

00:26:10.900 --> 00:26:20.620
that has come from experience quantitative techniques have not been provided could not

00:26:20.620 --> 00:26:32.010
be provided and these are just thumb rules. There is tradeoff between alternatives because

00:26:32.010 --> 00:26:40.520
when we design a software we have to look at various kinds of tradeoff the complexity

00:26:40.520 --> 00:26:49.610
of the software the cost and so on. And because of the tradeoff between alternatives

00:26:49.910 --> 00:27:01.120
we have a pragmatic approach to cost effectiveness. Just to summarize our discussion software engineering

00:27:01.120 --> 00:27:08.880
is actually an engineering approach to develop software and this engineering approach has

00:27:08.880 --> 00:27:18.220
developed from past experience of large number of programmers. Over the years the programmers

00:27:18.220 --> 00:27:25.360
have innovated new ways of looking at how to write program good programs and so on. All

00:27:25.360 --> 00:27:33.760
these techniques have been systematically organized so that somebody can go through these topics

00:27:34.260 --> 00:27:44.360
and be a good programmer be able to write large programs in a team and so on. So, that

00:27:44.360 --> 00:27:52.140
is the focus of our discussion and over the next few lectures we will discuss various

00:27:52.140 --> 00:27:57.580
techniques issues and so on. Thank you.

